ver and was taking no regular medication except recent (3 months) use of performance-enhancing drugs (PEDs) purchased from a fitness center, including two selective androgen receptor modulators (SARMs)—RAD140 5 mg twice daily and andarine 25 mg twice daily, 5 days per week—as well as the growth hormone (GH) secretagogue (GHS)/ghrelin analog ibutamoren 25 mg daily, 5 days per week. He had no previous use of hormonal supplements. The patient reported no serious disease apart from borreliosis in 2012, seasonal pollinosis, and minor injuries related to physical activities. Three years before this visit, he underwent a routine general check-up. At that time, his weight was... You do not currently have access to this content.}
